Since you're on an Ubuntu VM, the easiest way to open Grafana is with kubectl port-forward.

1. Check Grafana Service
Shell
kubectl get svc -n monitoring

You should see something like:

Plain Text
monitoring-grafana
2. Start Port Forward
Shell
kubectl port-forward -n monitoring svc/monitoring-grafana 3000:80 --address 0.0.0.0

Keep this terminal open.

3. Find Your VM IP
Shell
hostname -I

Example:

Plain Text
192.168.11.152
4. Open Grafana

From your laptop browser:

Plain Text
http://192.168.11.152:3000

or if you're on the VM desktop itself:

Plain Text
http://localhost:3000
5. Get Grafana Password
Shell
kubectl get secret -n monitoring monitoring-grafana \
-o jsonpath="{.data.admin-password}" | base64 -d && echo
6. Login
Plain Text
Username: admin
Password: <output from above command>
7. Verify Port 3000 is Listening

If the page doesn't open:

Shell
ss -tulpn | grep 3000

You should see:

Plain Text
LISTEN 0.0.0.0:3000
Useful Grafana Dashboards

After login:

Kubernetes / Compute Resources / Cluster
Kubernetes / Compute Resources / Node
Kubernetes / Compute Resources / Pod
Node Exporter Full

